  "lineage": "Israeli urban style formed in the 1970s among Yemenite, Iraqi, Moroccan and Turkish immigrant communities of south Tel Aviv and Jerusalem's Kerem HaTeimanim, circulated on kiosk cassettes ('musiqa qassetot') and codified by Zohar Argov, Daklon and arranger Moshe Ben-Mush — Hebrew lyrics sung with dense Arab-style silsulim melisma over 4/4 or 8/8 darbuka-and-bass grooves at 100-130 BPM, with electric guitar or bouzouki playing oud-derived maqam lines against synthesizer strings.",
